# Configuration file for the plustek8200i backend
#
# This backend drives the Genesys GL128 Plustek OpticFilm 8200i,
# USB 0x07b3/0x1825. The scanner is detected automatically and this file
# normally needs no changes.
#
# The older OpticFilm 8200i reports 0x07b3/0x130d and uses a GL845; it is
# handled by the genesys backend, not by this one.

# Device detection
# ----------------
# The built-in ID below is always probed, whether or not it appears here.
# Add a `usb VID PID' line to make the backend claim an additional ID --
# useful for a relabelled unit or a new revision that is otherwise
# identical. Values are hexadecimal.
#
# usb 0x07b3 0x1825

# A specific device node may be named directly if automatic detection
# fails:
#
# usb /dev/bus/usb/001/002

# Note: this backend implements no `option' settings. Scan parameters
# (mode, resolution, depth, infrared cleaning, exposure and the scan
# window) are SANE options, set per scan by the frontend -- see
# sane-plustek8200i(5). Any `option' line here is ignored and logged.
